A||N||3||86SEFIERO||temperature guage||||1||
Z||000000||86SEFIERO||02-08-2001||05:14 AM||||<BR>Guage was working fine then all of a sudden the next start-up it dont work,then it worked for a little while , now when I drove it home tonight the needle was pegged all te way up on the hotside to where I could barely see it. I know that the motors not running hot it's fine. What could be the problem? Thankyou!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Luperman||02-08-2001||08:36 AM||||It's a design error GM made in the wiring of the temp gauge, when you go to start the car 12 volts is applied to the gauge and it pegs all the way to hotttttt, there is a wiring fix for this just do a search for it here. good luck mine does this too till I tap on the gauge <P>------------------<BR>86 fiero SE 2M6        84 Grand Wagoneer 360||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||02-08-2001||09:38 AM||||You should also check the condition of the connector to the sensor.  It is easy to find at the rear of the engine near the coil on the V6.  It will have 2 wires to the sensor.  If the wire is bad or has come off, and is grounded the temp needle will peg.  <P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000003||c m west||02-09-2001||01:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 86SEFIERO:<BR><B><BR>Guage was working fine then all of a sudden the next start-up it dont work,then it worked for a little while , now when I drove it home tonight the needle was pegged all te way up on the hotside to where I could barely see it. I know that the motors not running hot it's fine. What could be the problem? Thankyou!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the temp guage is controled by a transducer <BR>located in the RIGHT cylinder head ( trunk side ) near the coil, if you remove the wires from the transducer with the ignition on and the gauge drops to cold then the transducer is at fault, if the needle is still peggeg hot when removed, check for a short in the wiring of the circuit, if no short is found then the guage is at fault<P>||||reg||1
